WEBVTT

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:33.440
SEPTEMBER 13, 1999

00:01:31.150 --> 00:01:35.740
This project is a light that will shine
upon the future of the 24th Ward.

00:01:36.070 --> 00:01:40.490
Twenty years from now, the 24th Ward
will be incorporated into Tokyo.

00:01:40.780 --> 00:01:44.700
That's when this island
will have no more accidents nor crime.

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:48.580
It'll be the model of an ideal city.
A "smart city."

00:01:48.580 --> 00:01:51.250
That'll be all thanks to your research here.

00:01:51.790 --> 00:01:53.630
Suido Zaibatsu will back you up.

00:01:54.170 --> 00:01:57.470
Ms. Kanae Isshiki, please lend us a hand.

00:01:58.970 --> 00:02:01.850
Oh no, the pleasure is all ours.

00:02:04.810 --> 00:02:07.390
We can't trust Gori Suido.

00:02:07.390 --> 00:02:08.770
You think so?

00:02:08.770 --> 00:02:10.150
He's coming from the mainland

00:02:10.150 --> 00:02:13.690
to use the 24th Ward as a guinea pig
because of its lax regulations.

00:02:13.940 --> 00:02:18.450
Verification of autonomous driving
that uses cloud computing in conjunction.

00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:20.240
He's 10 years ahead of others.

00:02:20.490 --> 00:02:24.700
I'm glad that we'll have a budget,
but it's too good to be true.

00:02:25.240 --> 00:02:28.250
Cautiousness is a good trait
that you have, Kuchikiri.

00:02:28.250 --> 00:02:30.620
I did grow up in Shantytown after all.

00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:34.380
You can't stop the flow of time.

00:02:34.710 --> 00:02:37.460
If information technology continues
to advance at the current rate,

00:02:37.460 --> 00:02:40.630
the world should be a completely different place
20 years from now.

00:02:43.970 --> 00:02:46.520
Aren't you afraid of change?

00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:49.730
Even if you're scared, the future will still come.

00:03:00.740 --> 00:03:02.870
O-Ow...

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:04.780
Kuchikiri, are you all right?

00:03:05.490 --> 00:03:08.040
Someone!
Someone, please call an ambulance!

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:15.420
Kuchikiri.

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:18.300
This is an accident. It's not your fault.

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:20.670
I'm the one who designed the program.

00:03:20.970 --> 00:03:26.560
My AI calculated the values of life
and chose him as the sacrifice.

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:27.810
Oh, no.

00:03:28.180 --> 00:03:31.060
Mr. Kuchikiri took my place?

00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:46.580
Kuchikiri?

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:50.870
Kanae? Where are we?

00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:53.790
A hospital. I'll call for someone.

00:03:57.380 --> 00:04:00.210
What day is it today?

00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:11.230
You can't read any letters?

00:04:11.230 --> 00:04:13.440
They said it's a type of dyslexia.

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:15.190
It's pretty amusing.

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:17.860
Bugs are dancing within my field of vision.

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:22.190
I'm sorry, it's my fault.

00:04:22.610 --> 00:04:24.450
It's nothing to worry about.

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:27.580
They said there have been cases
that heal over time.

00:04:27.990 --> 00:04:29.580
Besides, Sakiko...

00:04:29.950 --> 00:04:32.750
This may be a gift from god.

00:04:33.460 --> 00:04:35.250
From god?

00:04:35.540 --> 00:04:41.670
Until now, I devoted myself to research,
thinking technology will improve the future.

00:04:41.670 --> 00:04:45.470
But now, I see the world
in a completely different light.

00:04:46.260 --> 00:04:47.850
Can you lend me a pen?

00:04:49.930 --> 00:04:54.850
In my eyes right now, the kanji
for my own name, Kuchikiri, looks like this.

00:04:55.850 --> 00:04:57.860
Does that say 0th?

00:04:58.270 --> 00:05:02.030
Yes, 0th. That has a wonderful ring to it.

00:05:03.990 --> 00:05:07.620
Predictions of the future
are based on past data.

00:05:07.990 --> 00:05:10.910
What was dangerous in the past
will still be dangerous in the future.

00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:13.790
What was unnecessary in the past
will still be unnecessary in the future.

00:05:13.790 --> 00:05:17.000
Quantification will fortify preexisting values.

00:05:17.500 --> 00:05:21.460
However, human society has continued
to change, renovating its own past.

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:25.130
How people will live
cannot be decided solely from the past.

00:05:25.420 --> 00:05:29.140
I have to believe in the possibilities of the future,
from each and every person.

00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:33.770
But how can I quantify possibilities?

00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:35.810
Who will be held responsible?

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:38.600
To resolve that...

00:05:39.190 --> 00:05:40.310
But...

00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:42.980
Come in.

00:05:43.610 --> 00:05:44.860
Excuse me.

00:05:45.570 --> 00:05:47.110
Mr. Suido.

00:05:47.110 --> 00:05:49.990
It's not good to push yourself too hard.

00:05:50.490 --> 00:05:52.030
I'm sorry.

00:05:52.740 --> 00:05:58.080
I never want an accident like that
to happen ever again.

00:05:59.170 --> 00:06:03.000
Ms. Kanae, you are a genius
in information engineering.

00:06:03.130 --> 00:06:04.300
At a young age,

00:06:04.300 --> 00:06:08.630
you completed a rudimentary thesis for the Next
Generation Macroscopic Complex Computer.

00:06:08.930 --> 00:06:12.350
I do not doubt your abilities one bit.

00:06:12.350 --> 00:06:18.890
However, not even you, after trying this hard,
can find a method to solve this problem.

00:06:19.810 --> 00:06:25.940
Can that be because this system has a flaw
that cannot be overcome by principle?

00:06:26.150 --> 00:06:28.820
Even if that's the case, it doesn't matter.

00:06:29.110 --> 00:06:32.240
I destroyed Kuchikiri's future.

00:06:32.910 --> 00:06:37.500
So that something like this never happens again,
I must complete this system.

00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:41.170
Something can be born
from mistakes as well. See?

00:06:42.040 --> 00:06:43.170
Ms. Kanae!

00:06:43.670 --> 00:06:45.920
Ms. Kanae!

00:06:46.010 --> 00:06:47.380
Hey!

00:06:47.380 --> 00:06:48.920
Sakiko?

00:06:51.260 --> 00:06:53.220
It's done!

00:06:57.180 --> 00:06:58.560
Amazing.

00:06:58.850 --> 00:07:01.100
I feel a strong assertion coming from the art.

00:07:01.520 --> 00:07:03.480
Kuchikiri drew that?

00:07:03.650 --> 00:07:08.240
I hear he goes by the name "0th" lately.
He seems to have become quite the celebrity now.

00:07:08.740 --> 00:07:10.530
I didn't know that.

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:15.330
He doesn't regret the past,
nor does he have a grudge against you.

00:07:15.830 --> 00:07:18.080
He's looking into his own future.

00:07:18.540 --> 00:07:22.000
Ms. Kanae, you shouldn't be trapped
in the past, either.

00:07:22.420 --> 00:07:26.050
That should be how you atone for your sin.

00:07:29.590 --> 00:07:30.510
All right.

00:07:33.930 --> 00:07:36.810
MARCH 23, 2004

00:07:37.770 --> 00:07:39.270
Mrs. Suido.

00:07:39.890 --> 00:07:41.270
Sakiko.

00:07:41.270 --> 00:07:42.650
It's been a while.

00:07:42.650 --> 00:07:45.980
Time passes by so quickly.
Congratulations on your graduation.

00:07:46.940 --> 00:07:48.230
Thank you so much.

00:07:48.690 --> 00:07:53.660
With your help, I made it into Kokugou University
and was able to become one of your juniors.

00:07:53.950 --> 00:07:57.620
I will make sure to inherit all of your research.

00:07:58.040 --> 00:08:03.040
I said this many times, Sakiko,
but that accident was merely a catalyst.

00:08:03.040 --> 00:08:07.170
You don't have to feel responsible
for me quitting my research.

00:08:07.500 --> 00:08:08.670
No way.

00:08:08.840 --> 00:08:13.130
Without your research, I would not be alive.

00:08:13.340 --> 00:08:16.970
I want to repay everyone who I owe a debt to.

00:08:18.930 --> 00:08:20.100
I see.

00:08:20.930 --> 00:08:24.140
Ideally, I wanted to do the research
together with you.

00:08:25.190 --> 00:08:27.860
Why did you become a schoolteacher?

00:08:28.360 --> 00:08:30.230
I mean, it was so sudden.

00:08:30.440 --> 00:08:32.320
Did Mr. Gori influence you?

00:08:33.280 --> 00:08:35.280
Well, I guess that's part of it.

00:08:35.660 --> 00:08:39.790
Gori was always interested in education.

00:08:40.120 --> 00:08:43.620
He says he's going to create
a comprehensive K-12 school,

00:08:43.620 --> 00:08:46.290
and is currently making appeals
to various places.

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:48.880
But that's not all.

00:08:49.170 --> 00:08:52.050
I thought about something
while looking at 0th's graffiti.

00:08:52.300 --> 00:08:57.050
Sowing and reaping
are both very important jobs.

00:08:57.300 --> 00:08:59.430
My current job is to sow.

00:08:59.680 --> 00:09:01.930
I'll leave the reaping to you.

00:09:05.190 --> 00:09:07.560
INFORMATION ENGINEERING
PROF. MAKOTO KASUGA

00:09:06.480 --> 00:09:07.560
Good morning.

00:09:07.940 --> 00:09:10.730
I will be working here starting today.
My name is Sakiko Tsuzura—

00:09:11.780 --> 00:09:12.940
Huh?

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:16.490
Was I too early?

00:09:20.120 --> 00:09:21.290
You're the new girl?

00:09:22.830 --> 00:09:25.370
I'm sorry,
I must have entered the wrong room.

00:09:25.410 --> 00:09:28.000
Wait, hold on!
You probably came to the right place.

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:30.130
You definitely did. I'm sure of it.

00:09:30.210 --> 00:09:32.630
I have no interest in clubs
with strange activities.

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:37.640
This isn't part of my club activities.
It's just what I do for my part-time job.

00:09:37.720 --> 00:09:40.760
The lab has really bright fluorescent lights
so I couldn't sleep.

00:09:41.390 --> 00:09:42.850
I'm Wataru Chikushi.

00:09:43.100 --> 00:09:44.310
Nice to meet you, Satchan.

00:09:44.310 --> 00:09:45.850
Please call me Tsuzuragawa.

00:09:45.980 --> 00:09:47.310
So fast to reply.

00:09:47.600 --> 00:09:49.980
Well, why don't you sit there for now?

00:09:49.980 --> 00:09:51.110
You want some coffee?

00:09:51.320 --> 00:09:52.190
Yes, please.

00:09:52.900 --> 00:09:54.320
Satchan, you want it black?

00:09:54.320 --> 00:09:56.990
"Tsuzuragawa" would like some milk as well.

00:10:00.370 --> 00:10:01.530
Concerned about this?

00:10:01.830 --> 00:10:03.580
- Did you make it yourself?
- Yep!

00:10:03.580 --> 00:10:05.330
I burned the midnight oil to make it.

00:10:05.790 --> 00:10:08.580
Our local hero, Mr. 24.

00:10:08.580 --> 00:10:11.790
He'll protect the peace of 24th Ward,
24 hours a day.

00:10:13.300 --> 00:10:14.710
Your finishing touches are sloppy.

00:10:15.970 --> 00:10:17.970
I worked really hard on this, you know.

00:10:17.970 --> 00:10:21.260
Someone I know
would be able to make it more properly.

00:10:21.260 --> 00:10:24.180
What? You know a sculptor or something?

00:10:24.390 --> 00:10:27.140
But aren't place like that
ridiculously expensive, Satchan?

00:10:27.140 --> 00:10:28.350
I'm Tsuzuragawa.

00:10:28.730 --> 00:10:33.230
The person I know doesn't decide from price,
but by whether or not it's worth doing.

00:10:33.230 --> 00:10:37.740
If he resonates with how you really feel,
I'm sure he'll make it, even for free.

00:10:39.450 --> 00:10:41.280
Amazing.

00:10:41.910 --> 00:10:44.330
You made all these, 0th?

00:10:44.580 --> 00:10:46.580
My main art medium is graffiti, though.

00:10:46.870 --> 00:10:49.000
All right, done.

00:10:49.750 --> 00:10:51.420
What do you think of this design?

00:10:54.500 --> 00:10:55.710
Looks good.

00:10:55.710 --> 00:10:58.720
It feels like someone
who would fight evil 24 hours in a row.

00:10:58.720 --> 00:10:59.720
Right?

00:10:59.930 --> 00:11:03.180
Is the area around this horn
respect to Muscle Boy?

00:11:03.180 --> 00:11:07.930
Oh, you noticed? I wanted to put in
a bit of Japanese hero designs.

00:11:06.680 --> 00:11:09.810
I can't keep up when guys branch off like this.

00:11:09.810 --> 00:11:11.400
Huh? What's this?

00:11:11.560 --> 00:11:13.110
That's Carneades.

00:11:13.230 --> 00:11:17.400
I set him up to be a villain that mercilessly
demands the hero to make a decision.

00:11:17.480 --> 00:11:21.780
I see, that's pretty dramatic.

00:11:21.780 --> 00:11:23.950
All right, I'll use that too.

00:11:23.950 --> 00:11:27.040
Man, you've really helped me so much, 0th.

00:11:27.040 --> 00:11:28.870
Can you also make 3D versions as well?

00:11:29.250 --> 00:11:31.460
It's for the sake of a fellow Kasuga Lab alum.

00:11:31.460 --> 00:11:37.170
In return, it'd help me a lot if you take care
of Sakiko while I'm away from Japan.

00:11:37.460 --> 00:11:39.510
Going on a trip abroad?

00:11:39.920 --> 00:11:43.090
I want to touch upon real graffiti in New York.

00:11:43.090 --> 00:11:46.100
Fortunately, it looks like
I'll have financial support.

00:11:46.260 --> 00:11:47.810
New Yorker.

00:11:47.810 --> 00:11:49.560
Will you be all right by yourself?

00:11:50.020 --> 00:11:52.560
I can read simple letters now.

00:11:52.690 --> 00:11:55.110
- I can make do with daily life things.
- But...

00:11:55.110 --> 00:11:56.860
This is something I need.

00:11:57.780 --> 00:12:00.610
I stopped my research
because there was a revelation from god.

00:12:01.280 --> 00:12:04.160
Just like how you're trying
to change the world with programs,

00:12:04.700 --> 00:12:07.240
I'm going to change the world through art.

00:12:09.830 --> 00:12:14.380
Change the world through art.
I've never thought of things like that.

00:12:14.380 --> 00:12:18.630
But when I look at the pieces here,
I started to feel like you can do it.

00:12:18.750 --> 00:12:20.630
What will you do, Mr. Chikushi?

00:12:20.630 --> 00:12:21.970
Huh? Me?

00:12:22.340 --> 00:12:25.220
I will... Let's see.

00:12:25.590 --> 00:12:28.970
I might still be doing hero stuff
even after graduating from college.

00:12:29.180 --> 00:12:31.640
What? Will you be able to graduate?

00:12:36.900 --> 00:12:41.360
Golden Sunshine!

00:12:37.310 --> 00:12:39.940
OCTOBER 3, 2012

00:12:41.530 --> 00:12:44.150
It's been almost two years
since we started Takara Food Bank.

00:12:44.610 --> 00:12:49.030
It's been on the news as a model case
for regional interactions and volunteering.

00:12:49.450 --> 00:12:51.660
It's definitely becoming more prevalent.

00:12:51.660 --> 00:12:53.870
It's all thanks to everyone
on the shopping street.

00:12:53.870 --> 00:12:55.290
Mom!

00:12:55.460 --> 00:12:58.460
I got some Golden Sunrise. Here.

00:12:58.460 --> 00:13:00.250
Oh, thank you.

00:13:00.750 --> 00:13:02.670
You too, Dad. It's delicious.

00:13:03.220 --> 00:13:04.930
Yeah, thank you.

00:13:06.760 --> 00:13:07.640
Delicious.

00:13:08.100 --> 00:13:09.470
Right?

00:13:09.600 --> 00:13:12.100
Hey, Asumi, let's go.

00:13:12.100 --> 00:13:14.730
If you're dilly-dallying, we'll leave you behind.

00:13:14.730 --> 00:13:16.600
Oh, wait.

00:13:16.600 --> 00:13:19.900
Don't worry. We won't leave you behind.

00:13:17.190 --> 00:13:18.560
I'm glad.

00:13:18.560 --> 00:13:20.230
Huh? About what?

00:13:20.230 --> 00:13:25.740
Well, if I was still a researcher,
I'm sure I'd still be trapped in a distant ideal,

00:13:25.740 --> 00:13:28.740
unable to notice
all the people reaching out to me.

00:13:29.700 --> 00:13:34.040
Gori, thank you for giving me
encouragement back then.

00:13:34.120 --> 00:13:35.830
No, I have to thank you.

00:13:36.120 --> 00:13:40.790
I created Suido Academy
because of your decision, Kanae.

00:13:41.880 --> 00:13:44.090
But we still have so much to do.

00:13:44.380 --> 00:13:47.510
Yes, you're right. Things we need to do...
Huh?

00:13:49.680 --> 00:13:50.470
Kanae?

00:13:50.470 --> 00:13:53.020
Dear, I just remembered
I had to do something.

00:13:53.020 --> 00:13:55.480
Can you help with the cleanup without me?

00:13:55.600 --> 00:13:57.350
Huh? Sure.

00:13:59.270 --> 00:14:00.650
Hot. So hot.

00:14:00.900 --> 00:14:02.400
Good job out there.

00:14:02.400 --> 00:14:04.240
Is there anything else to carry?

00:14:04.240 --> 00:14:06.780
Sorry to make you help us out.

00:14:06.780 --> 00:14:08.240
It was Mrs. Kanae's request.

00:14:09.410 --> 00:14:11.330
You don't have to blush so much.

00:14:19.120 --> 00:14:23.250
Excuse me. You're here to see
the Food Bank, right? If you'd like...

00:14:23.250 --> 00:14:24.340
Wallet.

00:14:27.130 --> 00:14:28.720
Wallet.

00:14:30.800 --> 00:14:33.350
Um, how about we chat for a bit?

00:14:33.350 --> 00:14:37.690
Just shut up and give me your wallet!

00:14:43.570 --> 00:14:44.980
Chikushi? Are you okay?

00:14:50.200 --> 00:14:51.370
Kanae?

00:14:52.700 --> 00:14:53.910
Oh, no.

00:14:54.030 --> 00:14:55.160
Mr. Chikushi!

00:14:55.410 --> 00:14:58.540
Ms. Kanae is collapsed. What happened—

00:14:58.710 --> 00:15:00.960
Satchan, please, hurry and get an ambulance.

00:15:01.250 --> 00:15:03.250
You were here with her. What were you doing?

00:15:03.340 --> 00:15:06.010
The hospital is right there, so I'll take her.

00:15:07.210 --> 00:15:08.630
I'm trusting you, Satchan.

00:15:08.630 --> 00:15:11.590
- Mr. Chikushi, please go let Mr. Gori know.
- Yeah.

00:15:19.270 --> 00:15:20.390
Sakiko.

00:15:20.390 --> 00:15:22.400
It's all right. We'll be at a hospital soon.

00:15:22.400 --> 00:15:25.690
If I don't make it...

00:15:26.110 --> 00:15:29.400
Please take care of Koki and Asumi.

00:15:31.200 --> 00:15:36.200
OPERATING ROOM

00:15:36.620 --> 00:15:37.660
How is Ms. Kanae?

00:15:37.660 --> 00:15:39.290
- Are you a family member?
- No.

00:15:39.290 --> 00:15:40.920
- Kanae!
- Mr. Gori.

00:15:41.620 --> 00:15:42.670
Are you the husband?

00:15:43.250 --> 00:15:45.000
Please calm down and listen.

00:15:45.170 --> 00:15:49.050
Unfortunately, your wife
passed away moments ago.

00:15:49.340 --> 00:15:52.680
We did our best,
but she fell into shock due to blood loss.

00:16:11.700 --> 00:16:13.530
Interaction overcoming circumstances.

00:16:13.950 --> 00:16:17.700
A bridge to the future
built by people helping each other.

00:16:18.240 --> 00:16:20.450
The world that Kanae sought...

00:16:20.790 --> 00:16:22.960
The future I sought...

00:16:23.460 --> 00:16:25.540
was not supposed to be this.

00:16:26.170 --> 00:16:27.630
It definitely was not.

00:16:30.300 --> 00:16:33.180
I see, what Kanae tried to achieve was...

00:16:33.550 --> 00:16:38.180
If that system can be finished,
all crimes will be prevented beforehand,

00:16:38.260 --> 00:16:40.310
and incidents like this
won't have to happen at all.

00:16:40.720 --> 00:16:44.350
Tsuzuragawa, you took over
Kanae's research, didn't you?

00:16:45.350 --> 00:16:47.360
I beg you. I don't care how much it costs.

00:16:47.650 --> 00:16:49.820
I will take any blame that comes our way.

00:16:49.820 --> 00:16:53.400
So please finish Kanae's system.

00:16:53.400 --> 00:16:56.740
So that a tragedy like this
won't happen ever again.

00:16:59.740 --> 00:17:01.660
That's what I've always intended on doing.

00:17:02.450 --> 00:17:04.540
I have a request to make as well.

00:17:05.040 --> 00:17:10.210
Ms. Kanae asked me
to take care of Koki and Asumi.

00:17:10.300 --> 00:17:14.800
I would like to request permission
to periodically check how they're doing.

00:17:15.470 --> 00:17:17.470
SPECIAL ADMINISTRATIVE REGION GUARD

00:17:16.260 --> 00:17:18.930
APRIL 1, 2013

00:17:19.720 --> 00:17:20.560
Yo.

00:17:21.470 --> 00:17:24.100
Oh, sorry to surprise you.

00:17:25.480 --> 00:17:26.600
Why are you here?

00:17:26.810 --> 00:17:32.190
Employment. A job. Satchan, you were the one
who said I shouldn't loiter around forever.

00:17:32.320 --> 00:17:35.820
It's "Tsuzuragawa."
How long will you act like a college student?

00:17:36.280 --> 00:17:38.320
By chance, are we coworkers?

00:17:38.780 --> 00:17:40.490
We are not coworkers.

00:17:40.490 --> 00:17:44.870
We're just borrowing space for now.
I work for the Information Center.

00:17:45.210 --> 00:17:47.250
You're so cold.

00:17:50.210 --> 00:17:51.130
What's this?

00:17:51.130 --> 00:17:52.090
Please give that back.

00:17:55.510 --> 00:17:57.840
If I recall, that was...

00:17:59.760 --> 00:18:02.140
Oh hey, it's been a while.

00:18:02.600 --> 00:18:05.940
Oh, right. I'm doing well.

00:18:05.940 --> 00:18:07.850
I work at SARG now.

00:18:08.100 --> 00:18:10.900
SARG? You quit being a hero?

00:18:11.070 --> 00:18:15.490
<i>I couldn't protect an important person who was
right in front of me. I'm nowhere near a hero.</i>

00:18:16.240 --> 00:18:18.200
If I seriously want to protect others,

00:18:18.450 --> 00:18:19.990
<i>I have to grow up.</i>

00:18:20.410 --> 00:18:21.660
I see.

00:18:22.370 --> 00:18:26.830
When I get back, I need to be careful so I don't
get arrested for destruction of property.

00:18:27.750 --> 00:18:29.330
<i>I'll be waiting for you, cuffs at the ready.</i>

00:18:29.790 --> 00:18:31.880
<i>By the way, is Sakiko doing well?</i>

00:18:31.880 --> 00:18:35.380
Yeah. It looks like she somehow got over it.

00:18:35.460 --> 00:18:39.890
Right now, she's going to the ward's
Central Information Center from college.

00:18:40.550 --> 00:18:41.510
<i>What's up?</i>

00:18:42.140 --> 00:18:44.890
She seems to be planning something
with Mr. Gori.

00:18:45.060 --> 00:18:47.520
The blueprints for Cornucopia
that was in the lab...

00:18:52.020 --> 00:18:54.020
Hey, 0th?

00:18:54.020 --> 00:18:55.730
GORI SUIDO SUPPORTERS GROUP FORMATION PARTY

00:18:54.360 --> 00:19:01.120
All teachers here at Suido Academy
will be fully supporting Chairman Suido.

00:19:01.450 --> 00:19:08.080
Chairman Suido, who is running for the next
mayoral election, will like to say a few...

00:19:08.830 --> 00:19:11.670
Who are you? What do you want?

00:19:11.880 --> 00:19:14.170
Are you going to waste Kanae's will?

00:19:14.170 --> 00:19:17.300
Do you really think
that's for the better of the world?

00:19:17.300 --> 00:19:19.180
That system has a major flaw—

00:19:19.180 --> 00:19:20.760
You think I don't know that?

00:19:22.180 --> 00:19:25.180
I watched Kanae
from a place closer than anyone else.

00:19:25.390 --> 00:19:30.600
She agonized about abandoning her research
because it was a valuable system.

00:19:30.900 --> 00:19:32.810
Are you going to step off the path of humanity?

00:19:33.110 --> 00:19:35.610
I will always strive to do my best.

00:19:35.820 --> 00:19:38.650
Any faults can be overcome
with advances in technology.

00:19:38.860 --> 00:19:41.990
Tsuzuragawa is advancing the project
with the same intent.

00:19:42.360 --> 00:19:44.830
I have never believed you to begin with.

00:19:44.830 --> 00:19:49.790
You'll someday lie that this is for everyone's
happiness, and sell your soul to the devil.

00:19:52.210 --> 00:19:54.960
SEPTEMBER 18, 2019

00:19:53.540 --> 00:19:55.540
Is the KANAE System doing well?

00:19:55.540 --> 00:20:00.340
It was a rush job, but the underground
Information Center will soon begin construction.

00:20:00.470 --> 00:20:02.800
Any alternate methods for the biological brain?

00:20:03.640 --> 00:20:05.510
We still have no prospects.

00:20:05.800 --> 00:20:07.600
So it was no good after all.

00:20:08.430 --> 00:20:14.150
Only a human brain can act
as the core of the KANAE System.

00:20:14.310 --> 00:20:17.570
It is my responsibility
that we could not create an alternative brain.

00:20:17.940 --> 00:20:19.030
If push comes to shove...

00:20:19.030 --> 00:20:21.070
Don't think of anything foolish.

00:20:21.200 --> 00:20:24.660
If I could do that,
I would have done so long ago.

00:20:24.910 --> 00:20:27.540
But Kanae will not wish for that.

00:20:28.700 --> 00:20:30.200
She shouldn't be wishing for that.

00:20:31.410 --> 00:20:32.790
OFFICE ROOM

00:20:33.040 --> 00:20:34.040
Please.

00:20:34.250 --> 00:20:37.000
It's about the Takara Elementary School case.

00:20:38.380 --> 00:20:42.510
I told you before. An abandoned school
not under management is a dangerous place.

00:20:42.510 --> 00:20:43.630
Look at this.

00:20:43.970 --> 00:20:45.430
We all drew it together.

00:20:45.760 --> 00:20:46.600
This is...

00:20:46.680 --> 00:20:48.350
Everyone is amazing.

00:20:48.350 --> 00:20:53.440
They're coming up with all sorts of ideas
to preserve and reuse Takara Elementary School.

00:20:53.480 --> 00:20:56.860
I want you to support the Elementary School
Preservation movement as the mayor.

00:20:57.150 --> 00:20:57.940
However—

00:20:57.940 --> 00:21:02.360
Please. I'm sure this is something we need
for the 24th Ward.

00:21:04.160 --> 00:21:05.280
All right.

00:21:05.610 --> 00:21:08.160
Mr. Shirakaba has asked me, too.

00:21:08.370 --> 00:21:09.870
I will bring it up as an agenda.

00:21:09.870 --> 00:21:13.710
But I can't be responsible
for getting everyone to agree with it.

00:21:15.080 --> 00:21:16.830
Thank you, Dad.

00:21:18.880 --> 00:21:20.300
Is it all right?

00:21:20.590 --> 00:21:23.590
Weren't the redevelopment plans
already under way?

00:21:23.760 --> 00:21:27.010
Back when 0th was starting up
and SARG was chasing him around,

00:21:27.090 --> 00:21:30.430
there was a time when Kanae
strongly covered for him.

00:21:30.510 --> 00:21:32.020
I was reminded of that.

00:21:32.560 --> 00:21:35.900
She's like her mother,
and grew up to be a kind person.

00:21:36.440 --> 00:21:42.940
Yes. Perhaps she's the hope
for the 24th Ward.

00:21:44.150 --> 00:21:46.700
MAY 8, 2020

00:21:45.570 --> 00:21:46.360
Asumi!

00:21:46.700 --> 00:21:48.200
Asumi!

00:21:57.630 --> 00:22:02.380
Due to prolonged impaired consciousness,
a large portion of her brain remains inactive.

00:22:03.010 --> 00:22:05.300
Furthermore, with extensive physical injuries,

00:22:05.300 --> 00:22:09.390
all biological activities
may cease as early as tomorrow.

00:22:10.100 --> 00:22:11.720
Please brace yourself for the worst.

00:22:11.720 --> 00:22:15.390
Is there any way you can save her?

00:22:15.600 --> 00:22:18.350
Unfortunately,
not with our current medicine.

00:22:24.070 --> 00:22:26.110
This is a revelation.

00:22:26.650 --> 00:22:28.860
For the happiness of the people,

00:22:29.200 --> 00:22:32.450
I will turn Asumi
into the 24th Ward's guardian angel.

00:22:33.240 --> 00:22:35.910
Please forgive me, Kanae.

00:22:39.540 --> 00:22:42.590
This is my belief.

00:22:42.880 --> 00:22:47.010
We have to have
a better future, Mrs. Kanae.

00:22:47.220 --> 00:22:49.050
No, Lady Kanae.

00:22:49.800 --> 00:22:53.310
Please forgive my sinful self.

00:23:25.800 --> 00:23:27.590
YEAR 2021

00:23:38.430 --> 00:23:40.560
No... Mari...

00:23:40.770 --> 00:23:44.820
But no matter which one you choose,
someone will not be saved.

00:23:45.070 --> 00:23:47.360
I can't make the choice.

00:23:47.940 --> 00:23:48.990
Help me.

00:23:48.990 --> 00:23:50.200
RGB.

00:23:50.610 --> 00:23:52.570
Help me, Shuta.
